        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_trigonometry_m03_l02"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Replace $2\\tan\\theta = \\frac{2\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ and cross-multiply.",
        "Show $2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 2\\sin^2\\theta + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta \\implies \\cos^2\\theta = 2\\sin^2\\theta$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express $\\tan\\theta$ as $\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ on the right-hand side:\n$$\\frac{2\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta} = \\frac{2\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$$",
        "Cross-multiply both sides:\n$$\\cos\\theta(2\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta) = 2\\sin\\theta(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta)$$",
        "Expand and simplify:\n$$2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 2\\sin^2\\theta + 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$$\n$$\\cos^2\\theta = 2\\sin^2\\theta$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_s17_13_q5_ii",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_trigonometry",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_trigonometry_m04_l02"
      },
      "hints": [
        "From $\\cos^2\\theta = 2\\sin^2\\theta$, deduce $\\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$.",
        "Solve in $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$ to get $\\theta = 35.3^\\circ, 144.7^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Divide both sides by $\\cos^2\\theta$:\n$$\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\approx \\pm 0.707107$$",
        "Solve for $\\theta$ in the interval $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$:\n$$\\theta_1 = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\approx 35.26^\\circ \\approx 35.3^\\circ$$\n$$\\theta_2 = 180^\\circ - 35.26^\\circ \\approx 144.74^\\circ \\approx 144.7^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 35.3^\\circ, \\quad 144.7^\\circ)$$"
      ]
    }
  ]
